/**
 * TypeScript mirror of the Meridian backend API contract.
 *
 * Source of truth: `backend/src/meridian/schemas/api.py` and the schema modules it imports
 * (`research`, `findings`, `citations`, `analysis`, `financials`, `report`, `events`, `enums`,
 * `telemetry`, `state`). Field names and enum string values match the backend exactly. This file is
 * generated by hand, not by a codegen tool, so keep it in lockstep with the backend if either side
 * changes.
 *
 * Conventions used when translating Pydantic -> TypeScript:
 *  - `datetime` / `date` fields are ISO-8601 strings on the wire; typed here as `IsoDateTime` / `IsoDate`
 *    (both plain `string` aliases) rather than `Date`, since JSON never carries `Date` objects.
 *  - `T | None` -> `T | null`. Fields with a Pydantic default (default_factory or scalar default) are
 *    still required here because the backend always serialises them.
 *  - `StrEnum` -> a string-literal union (not a TS `enum`) so values compare directly against JSON.
 */

